Introduction — Literature Review
Cyber Essentials (CE) provides a government-backed baseline for information security in UK organisations (NCSC, 2023). However, evidence indicates that small and medium enterprises often struggle to interpret and implement CE controls due to limited technical expertise, resource constraints, and competing priorities (Small Business Commissioner, 2023; Von Solms & Van Niekerk, 2013). This literature review summarises official guidance, academic studies and industry tools to identify the key barriers SMEs face and to justify the design choices for the Tanasiom Aegis toolkit.
